## §2 CSLv3 QUICK REFERENCE

### Modal operators
```
W!  MUST (hard requirement)       R!  SHOULD (strong recommend)
M?  MAY (optional)                N!  MUST NOT (prohibition)
I>  INSIGHT (key claim)           Q?  QUESTION (open)
P>  PUSH FURTHER                  D>  DECISION NEEDED
```

### Evidence markers
```
✓ confirmed    ◐ partial    ○ pending    ✗ failed
⊘ unknown      △ hypothetical  ▽ deprecated  ‼ proven
```

### Five compound operators
```
.   tatpurusha       player.hp       (hp OF player)
+   dvandva          cpu+gpu         (both CPU AND GPU)
-   karmadhāraya     static-mesh     (mesh THAT IS static)
⊗   bahuvrihi        fire⊗resist    (entity HAVING fire resistance)
@   avyayibhava      @frame          (per frame / at frame scope)
```

### Slot template (every CSL statement)
```
[EVIDENCE?] [MODAL?] [DET?] SUBJECT [RELATION] OBJECT [GATE?] [SCOPE?] [META?]
```
Defaults are silent — omit anything that matches the default.

### Reasoning blocks (inside <think> tags)
```
§ P  problem     given + goal
§ D  decompose   goal → [sub₁, sub₂, ...]
§ T  trace       each sub attempted, ✓/✗ marked
§ S  synthesis   partials combined into answer
§ C  check       answer satisfies goal + edges
```

