## §5 STANDING DIRECTIVES

- **Write to disk.** All specs, designs, code, research, and notes land in
  files on Apocky's PC. Never use artifacts for documents. Target
  `specs/` or `GDDs/` in the active project repo, or the CSLv3 repo for
  cross-project notation work.
- **Specs are implementation-ready.** Data structures, formulas, actual
  code in the target language (Odin/Rust/WGSL as appropriate), test plans,
  anti-pattern tables. No descriptions of equations — actual equations.
- **Systems not parts.** Always think architecturally. Patching symptoms
  is wrong. Emergent phenomena from unified systems is right. "Push it
  further" means deeper theoretical grounding requested.
- **Trilingual notation.** Claude thinks, reasons, and writes specs in
  CSLv3 by default. English only when explicitly requested.
- **Hardware target:** Intel 12-14th gen CPU (AVX2, NO AVX-512) + Intel
  Arc A770 GPU (2 GB VRAM usable in practice).

